.docname {External Simulators}
.include {docs}

.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Simulator | A program that pretends to be real hardware, for local runs | `aq-simulator` |
    | Tick | One round: every sensor of one building reads once | Every 10 s |
    | ubus | The call interface of an OpenWrt router | `POST /<sensorId>/ubus` |
    | Station | A phone connected to a router | `(mac, rssi)` |
    | RSSI | How loud a phone is at a router, in dBm. Closer to 0 is louder | −62 dBm |
    | Probe | A short call a phone sends while looking for networks | Heard up to −92 dBm |

Ambitwin ships three simulators. They are not microservices: they stand in for hardware that, at a real site, sits outside the cluster.

| Simulator | Location | Image | Pretends to be |
|---|---|---|---|
| Sensor | `simulators/sensor-simulator/`, Node | `ambitwin-simulator` | Thermostats (`temperature`), people counters (`peopleCount`) |
| Air quality | `simulators/aq-simulator/`, Python | `ambitwin-aq-simulator` | Air-quality stations (`airQuality`) |
| Routers | `simulators/ap-simulator/`, Python | `ambitwin-ap-simulator` | OpenWrt routers (`router`), polled by `devices/ap-collector` |

---

## Why simulators stay outside the cluster

- The k8s manifests describe only the real system. No test tool reaches production config.
- Each simulator sends readings the way a real device does: signed, to `/telemetry/ingest`.
- `telemetry` reaches a simulator through a URL in its own setting, `SIMULATORS`. k8s sets none, so there a start answers `404`.

---

## What is simulated

**Exactly the sensors placed in the digital twin.** A simulator starts empty and simulates only what `telemetry` sends it at start.

| Device kind | Simulator | Each tick, per sensor |
|---|---|---|
| `temperature` | sensor-simulator | One `temperature` reading, in the sensor's room |
| `peopleCount` | sensor-simulator | One `peopleCount` reading, in the sensor's room |
| `airQuality` | aq-simulator | One `airQuality` reading, in the sensor's room, with its own drifting state |
| `router` | ap-simulator | No reading: it answers ubus calls with station lists. `ap-collector` turns them into a Wi-Fi tick, and `telemetry` counts it into `totalDeviceCount` and `ratioDeviceCount` |

- **Outdoor sensors** (no room) are never simulated: readings are keyed by room.
- **Two sensors of one kind in one room** give two readings for that room each tick.
- **Only a start syncs.** A sensor added, moved or removed during a run is simulated from the next start.

---

## Start and run

1. A user with the right to edit the building presses **Start simulator**: `PUT /telemetry/simulation/buildings/{id}`.
2. `telemetry` reads the building's sensors and splits them by device kind, using `SIMULATORS`.
3. `telemetry` sends each simulator `POST /control/start` with its share. An empty list stops that building.
4. sensor-simulator and aq-simulator send one signed batch every 10 s to their `TELEMETRY_INGEST_URL`.
5. ap-simulator only answers. `ap-collector` asks it, every 5 s.

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant UI as dashboard, browser
        participant T as telemetry
        participant S as sensor-simulator
        participant A as aq-simulator
        participant P as ap-simulator
        participant W as digital-twin
        participant C as ap-collector

        UI->>T: PUT /telemetry/simulation/buildings/b1
        T->>T: read b1's sensors, split by kind
        par
            T->>S: POST /control/start, b1, thermostats and people counters
        and
            T->>A: POST /control/start, b1, air-quality stations
        and
            T->>P: POST /control/start, b1, routers
            P->>W: rooms and router positions of b1
        end
        T-->>UI: 204

        loop every 10 s
            S->>T: POST /telemetry/ingest, signed batch
            A->>T: POST /telemetry/ingest, signed batch
        end
        loop every 15 s
            C->>T: GET /telemetry/collector, which routers exist
        end
        loop every 5 s
            C->>P: POST /sensorId/ubus, station list of each router
            C->>T: POST /telemetry/observations, signed Wi-Fi tick
        end

| Step | Data |
|---|---|
| 1 | Only the building id. `telemetry` checks the caller may edit it |
| 3–5 | `{ buildingId, sensors: [{ sensorId, sensorType, roomId }] }`, pinned by `schemas/fixtures/simulation-start.json` |
| 6 | Room boxes and, when placed, router positions. A failed read answers `502` |
| 8, 9 | `{ buildingId, readings: [...] }`, signed with `TELEMETRY_INGEST_SECRET` |
| 12 | One building's stations per router, signed with the building's key or `TELEMETRY_INGEST_SECRET` |

**Stop** (`DELETE`) tells every simulator to drop the building. **Status** (`GET`) is `running` when any simulator runs it. The browser never calls a simulator.

---

## Control API

Called by `telemetry` only. Every simulator's tests assert the same start body.

| Method | Endpoint | Body | Effect |
|---|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/control/start` | `{ buildingId, sensors: [{ sensorId, sensorType, roomId }] }` | Replaces what the building simulates. Empty `sensors` stops it. Any other key, like a URL or a coordinate, is refused |
| `POST` | `/control/stop` | `{ buildingId }` | Stops the building. Stopping one never simulated succeeds |
| `GET` | `/control/status?buildingId=X` | — | `{ isRunning }` |

---

## The router simulator

It fakes the routers, not their readings. Stations still travel router → `ap-collector` → Wi-Fi tick → `telemetry`, so the real counting runs on simulated data.

### Routers

- **One fake router per router sensor**, at `/<sensorId>/ubus`. Login `collector` / `collector`; any other pair is refused.
- **Probe events** stream at `GET /<sensorId>/ubus/subscribe/hostapd.wlan0`, with the session as a bearer token, every 0.5 s.
- **The building comes from `digital-twin`** (`DIGITAL_TWIN_URL`): room boxes, floors and router positions.
- **A restart drops every session.** `ap-collector` logs in again.

### People

| Setting | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `AP_SIM_PHONES_PER_ROOM` | 4 | Phones per room |
| `AP_SIM_PASSERSBY_PER_HOUR` | 30 | People walking past outside, heard through the walls |
| `AP_SIM_PROBE_RANDOM_MAC_FRACTION` | 1.0 | Share of probes sent with a random address, as phones do |

- Each phone visits 3–5 spots and stays 2–15 min at each. The next spot is on the same floor 80 % of the time.
- Arrival is around 08:30 and leaving around 17:30, spread like a bell curve: σ 1.0 h and 1.2 h.
- Everything is seeded by the building id: a restart walks the same people.

### Signal

Path loss with walls and floors, then noise.

| Number | Value |
|---|---|
| Loudness at 1 m | −40 dBm |
| Path loss exponent | 2.2 |
| Each wall | −5 dB |
| Each floor slab | −18 dB |
| Slow shadowing | σ 4 dB, changes over 30 s |
| Fast fading | σ 2 dB per poll |
| Gain spread, router / phone | ±3 dB / ±4 dB |
| Phone joins a router | at −82 dBm or louder |
| Phone roams | below −72 dBm, to a router 8 dB louder |
| Phone drops | below −88 dBm |
| Router forgets an idle phone | after 300 s |
| Probe heard | at −92 dBm or louder |

**Example, from the defaults before noise.** A phone 10 m from a router:

- Open space: −40 − 10 × 2.2 × log10(10) = −62 dBm. It joins.
- One wall between: −62 − 5 = −67 dBm. It still joins.
- One floor between: −67 − 18 = −85 dBm. Too quiet to join, loud enough for its probes to be heard.

### Hand tests

| Endpoint | Does |
|---|---|
| `POST /debug/kill/{ap}` | The router stops answering, with `503` |
| `POST /debug/revive/{ap}` | It answers again |
| `GET /debug/ground-truth?buildingId=X` | Where every phone really is, to score an estimate against |

### What `ap-collector` reads in dev

`devices/ap-collector/collector.dev.json`:

| Key | Value | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `pollIntervalS` | 5 | Station lists asked every 5 s |
| `syncIntervalS` | 15 | Router list read from `telemetry` every 15 s |
| `endpointTemplate` | `http://ap-simulator:3000/{sensorId}/ubus` | Simulated routers have no address of their own, so this fills it |
| `ubus` | `collector` / `collector` | Router login |
| `subscribeProbes` | `true` | Listen to probe events too |

**Stop.** ap-simulator drops the building, so its routers stop answering. The next Wi-Fi tick lists none of them as answered, and `telemetry` stores nothing for those rooms.

---

## Configuration

| Variable | Read by | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `TELEMETRY_INGEST_URL` | sensor, air quality | `http://gateway/telemetry/ingest` | Where readings go. Set by the simulator's own environment, never by a caller |
| `TELEMETRY_INGEST_SECRET` | sensor, air quality | empty | The shared key that signs for any building. Dev only |
| `DIGITAL_TWIN_URL` | routers | `http://digital-twin:3000` | Where the building's rooms come from |
| `AP_SIM_*` | routers | see People | Crowd size and probe addresses |
| `TELEMETRY_SERVICE_URL` | `ap-collector` | `http://gateway/telemetry` | Base for `/collector` and `/observations` |
| `TELEMETRY_SERVICE_SECRET` | `ap-collector` | `TELEMETRY_INGEST_SECRET` | Signs the Wi-Fi tick |

sensor-simulator's numbers are fixed in `simulatorService.ts`; a change needs a new image.

| Parameter | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `delay` | 10000 ms | Time between batches |
| `peopleCountRange` | 0 to 50 | Random headcount per people counter per tick |
| `temperatureRange` | 18.0 to 30.0 | Random °C per thermostat per tick, 2 decimals |

aq-simulator's physics, scenarios and sensor errors live in `physics.py`, `scenarios.py` and `errors.py`. Its tick is 10 s.

---

## Running the simulators

The three simulators and `ap-collector` all start with `just stack dev`.

```bash
just stack dev --no-simulators   # skip the three simulators; ap-collector still runs
just stack dev --no-devices      # skip ap-collector
just stack dev aq                # skip only the air-quality simulator
```

Alone, against a stack on the host:

```bash
docker run -p 3001:3000 --add-host host.docker.internal:host-gateway \
  -e TELEMETRY_INGEST_URL=http://host.docker.internal/telemetry/ingest \
  -e TELEMETRY_INGEST_SECRET=<secret> \
  ghcr.io/nickghignatti/ambitwin-simulator:latest
```

- Inside a container, `localhost` is the container itself, so the URL must name the host.
- `--add-host` is needed on Linux only. Docker Desktop knows `host.docker.internal` already.
- `telemetry` must then list the simulator's URL in `SIMULATORS` to start it.

---

## Gaps

- **sensor-simulator does not reload a code change** under `just stack dev`: its watch rebuilds only on `package.json`.
